New ESP32 files will be displayed on browser refresh, both uploaded
and locally created. Files with a '.html' and '.foo' are ignored
and will not be displayed.

ESP32 files can be  downloaded with a right-click -> 'Save link as...'
text files are viewed with a click. Browser may block files with certain
extensions. Check download history if there are issues.

Directory hierarchy handling is not supported, only 'root' 
directory files shown for both ESP32 and  card.

There are 'trim()' and 'toUpperCase()' functions used 
when processing the commands below, case and 
spaces are set to a known state.

Input command...:
COUNTER:n - new value for start of counter, negative works too. 
            Ceiling and floor values not tested.            

LED:ON - Turns on LED_BUILTIN.

LED:OFF - Turns off LED_BUILTIN.

SD_DELETE:<filename> - Delete provided SD filename, case sensitive.  
                       Wrong name causes no error. 'DELETE' is permanent, 
                       be cautious.

SD_MOUNT - Mounts the SD card after insertion.

SD_REMOVE - Allows SD card to be safely removed, unmounted.

CLEAR - Clear log output box.

COUNTER_SAVE - Saves the current counter value to 'counter.dat' on LittleFS
               partition. Will allow for continued value to continue if planned
               power/reset occurs. Power outage not accommodated, the a user 
               driven initiative. 'counter.dat' can be manual added 
               to data directory, if needed. Or, a new 'counter.dat' will be 
               created on startup and set to 0.

Webpage button:
SD files - Shows SD card files in new browser page.

